          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong De Morgan topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a middle thing between a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical internal logic
            and a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            with an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic internal logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            obey a weak form of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
            which defines a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+Heyting+algebra"} De Morgan Heyting algebra
          %p
            The de Morgan property has many equivalent formulations and many facets making the class of de Morgan toposes an important one in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            %em extremally disconnected spaces
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is called a
            %strong De Morgan topos
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is an internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+Heyting+algebra"} De Morgan Heyting algebra
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
                is a De Morgan topos.
            %li
              %p
                A simple example of a topos that is De Morgan but not Boolean is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+topos"} Sierpinski topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\to}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                is easily seen to satify the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ore+condition"} Ore condition
                (cf.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#presheaf-deMorgan"} below
            %li
              %p
                The topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
                of sheaves on a topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is De Morgan precisely iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremally+disconnected+topological+space"} extremally disconnected
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\to}
                is equivalently the topos of sheaves on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+space"} Sierpinski space
                it instantiates this case as well.)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+topos"} Injective Grothendieck toposes
                are De Morgan (cf.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone 2002, p.739
          %h2#some_equivalent_formulations Some equivalent formulations
          %p The importance of the concept of a De Morgan topos stems partly from the fact that for many statements whose classical (Boolean) validity is lost in intuitionistic logic the De Morgan property delineates precisely the range of toposes where the statement is valid. An illustration of this is e.g. the implication that maximal ideals are prime in commutative rings.
          %p Though such statements are in fact equivalent to the De Morgan property they are better viewed as higher-order properties of De Morgan toposes.
          %p
            In contrast, there exists also a long list, mostly due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone79"} Johnstone (1979)
          #deMorgan_equivalents.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              be a topos. The following are equivalent:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                  is a De Morgan topos.
              %li
                %p
                  For all formulae
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi φ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi,\psi
                  \:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi φ
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi φ
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\models \neg (\varphi\wedge\psi)\Leftrightarrow(\neg\varphi\vee\neg\psi)
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  For every formula
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                  \:
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mo ¬
                          %mi φ
                          %mo ∨
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo ¬
                          %mi φ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\models \neg\varphi\vee\neg\neg\varphi
              %li
                %p
                  For every subobject
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ↣
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\rightarrowtail Y
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ¬
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∨
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo ¬
                          %mi X
                          %mo =
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg X\vee\neg\neg X=Y
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
                  is a De Morgan Heyting algebra for every
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℰ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in\mathcal{E}
              %li
                %p
                  The canonical monomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ⊤
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ↣
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mo ¬
                            %mo ¬
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\top,\bot):1\coprod 1\rightarrowtail\Omega_{\neg\neg}
                  to the subobject classifier of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sh
                          %mrow
                            %mo ¬
                            %mo ¬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
                  is an isomorphism.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mo ¬
                            %mo ¬
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{\neg\neg}
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+object"} decidable
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\coprod 1
                  is a retract of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mo ¬
                              %mo ¬
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{\neg\neg}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\coprod 1
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  = succeed "-sheaf" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo ¬
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi Ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot:1\to\Omega
                  has a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers+object"} object of Dedekind reals
                  coincides with the object of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind-MacNeille+completion"} Dedekind-MacNeille reals
          %p
            The first few equivalences are based mainly on the validity of the “law of excluded middle” for elements of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg a
            in any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+Heyting+algebra"} De Morgan Heyting algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone (2002, pp.999-1000)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone79"} Johnstone (1979)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The following shows that ‘being De Morgan’ is a
            %em local property
            i.e. stable under slicing. This is immediate from the fact that the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{E}/A
            sending
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_A: X\times A\to A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical
            hence preserves the various equivalent formulations of De Morgan’s law.
          #local_property.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be an object of the De Morgan topos
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slice topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/A
              is De Morgan as well.
          #presheaf-deMorgan.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a small category. The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{C}^{op}}
              is De Morgan precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              satifies the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ore+condition"} Ore condition
          %p
            This result due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Peter Johnstone
            appears e.g. in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone79"} Johnstone (1979)
            %a{:href => "#KR94"} Kock-Reyes (1994)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Caramello12"} Caramello (2012)
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+topology"} dense topology
            coincides with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+site"} atomic topology
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            satisfying the Ore condition the preceding proposition implies that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation subtopos
            of a De Morgan presheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{C}^{op}}
            is always
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+topos"} atomic
          %h3#de_morganization De Morganization
          %p
            It was discovered by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"} Olivia Caramello
            that every topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            can be associated with a De Morgan topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morganization"} De Morganization
          #largest_deMorgan.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Given a topos
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} dense subtopos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              that is a De Morgan topos.
          %p
            For a proof see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Caramello09"} Caramello (2009)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            that occurs here, refers to the
            %em De Morgan topology
            , cf.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morganization"} De Morganization
          %p
            As
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
            , is the
            %em smallest
            dense De Morgan subtopos, we see that all dense De Morgan subtoposes lie in the interval between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{m}(\mathcal{E})
          %p
            In analogy with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+geometric+morphism"} skeletal geometric morphisms
            that preserve
            = succeed "-sheaves," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{E}
            that map
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            to
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            are called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            = succeed "." do
              %em -skeletal
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morganization"} De Morganization
          #deMorgan_m-skeletal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              A topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is De Morgan iff every geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{E}
              is
              = succeed "-skeletal." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ▪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \qed
          %h3#the_gleason_cover The Gleason cover
          %p
            Another way to associate a De Morgan topos to an arbitrary topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            was proposed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Peter Johnstone
            in the late 70s (Johnstone
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone79b"} 1979b
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#J80"} 1980
            %em Gleason cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\mathcal{E}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            generalizes a construction in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            that covers an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            by an extremally disconnected topological space.
          %p ……
          %h3#relation_to_cohesion Relation to cohesion
          %p
            Given that the
            %a{:href => "#deMorgan_equivalents"} above conditions
            concern
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\coprod 1
            and the contractability of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{\neg\neg}
            it comes as no surprise that the De Morgan property interacts interestingly with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} Lawvere's
            axiomatic approach to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            and, in particular, with the part of it that concerns the connectedness of the subobject classifier in a cohesive topos of spaces. A first indication of this is the following:
          #omega_connected.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{C}^{op}}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
              is connected iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in Set^{\mathcal{C}^{op}}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              object and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{C}^{op}}
              is not de Morgan iff there exists a connected object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in Set^{\mathcal{C}^{op}}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\coprod 1\rightarrowtail X
              \.
          %p
            This result appears in
            %a{:href => "#RZZZ04"} La Palme-Reyes-Reyes-Zolfaghari (2004, p.220)
            where it is attributed to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} Lawvere
          %p
            The following result due to
            %a{:href => "#Mielke84"} Mielke (1984)
            shows that the De Morgan property coincides with the (local) absence of a non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval objects
            in a topos.
          %p
            Here by an interval object we mean an internal linearly ordered object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            with disjoint least and greatest elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:1\to I
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M:1\to I
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          %p
            An interval object is
            %em trivial
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\simeq I_1\coprod I_2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m,M
            factor through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_1,I_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is said to be
            %strong homotopically trivial
            if every interval object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is trivial,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is said to
            %em locally homotopically trivial
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slice topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
            is homotopically trivial for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in\mathcal{E}
          #deMorgan_interval.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              A topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is locally homotopically trivial iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is a De Morgan topos. If subobjects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              generate, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is homotopically trivial iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is a De Morgan topos.
          %p
            For situations where subobjects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            generate see e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone77"} Johnstone (1977, sec.5.3 pp.145ff)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(L)
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a{:href => "#Borceux94"} Borceux (1994, p.443)
            it follows then that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(L)
            %em is homotopically trivial
            precisely when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em De Morgan locale
          %h3#relation_to_model_theory Relation to model theory
          %p ….
          #model_companion.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              be a coherent theory. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              admits a
              %span.newWikiWord
                model companion
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/model+companion"} ?
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(\mathcal{T})
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amalgamation+property"} amalgamation property
              iff for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\in\mathcal{T}
              , the lattice of subobjects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              admits a negation satisfying
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A\vee\neg\neg A = B
          %p
            This result appears without proof in
            %a{:href => "#Harun96"} Harun (1976, p.73)
            where it is attributed to a preprint of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gonzalo+E.+Reyes"} Gonzalo E. Reyes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amalgamation+property"} amalgamation property
